---
import LegalDocument from '~/components/LegalDocument.astro';
import { company, siteVisitPolicyPageMeta } from '~/data/legal';

const updated = '14 September 2026';
const lead = `How we quote remotely and when a paid domestic site visit or commercial survey may apply. Last updated: ${updated}.`;
---
<LegalDocument
  title={siteVisitPolicyPageMeta.title}
  description={siteVisitPolicyPageMeta.description}
  heading="Site visit & quotation policy"
  lead={lead}
>
  <p>
    At <strong>{company.legalName}</strong>, we aim to provide accurate and professional quotations
    based on the individual requirements of each project.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where sufficient photographs, measurements and project information can be provided remotely, we
    may be able to provide an initial estimate without the need for a site visit.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where an on-site assessment is required to prepare an accurate quotation, a site visit or survey
    fee may apply.
  </p>

  <h2 class="legal-page__h2">Domestic site visit &amp; quotation</h2>
  <p>
    Where a domestic project requires an on-site assessment, measurement or detailed inspection, a
    site visit fee of <strong>£60 + VAT</strong> may apply.
  </p>
  <p>This may include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Travel time and fuel costs</li>
    <li>Assessment of the areas requiring work</li>
    <li>Measurements where required</li>
    <li>Review of surface condition and preparation requirements</li>
    <li>Discussion of finishes and specifications</li>
    <li>Preparation of a written quotation</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Where a site visit fee applies, an invoice will be issued in advance.</p>
  <p>
    The invoice must be paid in full before the appointment is confirmed and before{' '}
    {company.legalName} attends the property.
  </p>
  <p>
    If the quoted works are subsequently awarded to {company.legalName}, the full site visit fee
    will be credited against the agreed contract value.
  </p>

  <h2 class="legal-page__h2">Commercial site survey &amp; quotation</h2>
  <p>
    Where a commercial project requires an on-site inspection, measurements, access assessment,
    coating specification or detailed quotation, a commercial site survey fee of{' '}
    <strong>£100 + VAT</strong> may apply.
  </p>
  <p>This may include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Travel time and fuel costs</li>
    <li>Site inspection and measurements</li>
    <li>Assessment of existing surfaces and coatings</li>
    <li>Preparation requirements</li>
    <li>Access and equipment requirements</li>
    <li>Discussion of the required specification</li>
    <li>Preparation of a detailed quotation</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Where a commercial survey fee applies, an invoice will be issued in advance.</p>
  <p>
    The invoice must be paid in full before the appointment is confirmed and before{' '}
    {company.legalName} attends site.
  </p>
  <p>
    If the quoted works are subsequently awarded to {company.legalName}, the full commercial survey
    fee will be credited against the agreed contract value.
  </p>
  <p>
    For larger, specialist or technically complex projects requiring extensive surveying,
    specification work or multiple visits, an alternative survey fee may be agreed in advance.
  </p>

  <h2 class="legal-page__h2">Important</h2>
  <p>
    Any paid site visit or survey fee is <strong>fully credited</strong> against the agreed
    contract value if the customer proceeds with {company.legalName}.
  </p>
</LegalDocument>
